  "notes": "SOURCE: Official USF Bellini College of Engineering 4-year plan PDF, 'Computer Science B.S.C.S. - 120 credits, 2025/2026 Catalog', https://www.usf.edu/engineering/student-services/documents/4yrplan-computerscience.pdf (dated 6/2025; the plan itself states 'the catalog is the definitive source of requirements' and references https://cloud.usf.edu/catalog/undergrad/computersciencebscs). Catalog year recorded as 2025-2026, the ACTUAL catalog year printed on the source (not 2026-2027). TRANSCRIPTION: term-by-term transcription of the official plan; course titles verified against the official 2025-2026 Undergraduate Catalog program page (catalog.usf.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=23&poid=11533), which confirms TOTAL DEGREE HOURS: 120, the 59-credit major core, and 21 credits of major electives (9 software + 3 theory + 9 additional non-overlapping technical from the approved Bellini College list). CAVEATS: (1) Courses marked with * in the source (MAC 2311, COP 2510, PHY 2048/2048L, COP 3514, COT 3100, CDA 3103) require a minimum grade of B (not B-) to meet prerequisites for the next course; unless otherwise stated, the minimum acceptable grade in all BSCS required courses is a C (C- insufficient). (2) Students apply for progression to upper division at the end of the Spring semester of Year 1 (requirements: ability to register for COP 4530, minimum 2.0 overall and USF GPA; 2.0 semester/math-science/specialization/USF/overall GPAs must be maintained; required math, science, engineering and specialization courses allowed max two registered attempts). (3) The college recommends an industry internship (up to 6 hrs of CIS 4940 may count as elective; no more than 3 hrs per company) — transcribed as an optional 0-credit advisory Summer Year 3 slot. (4) Exit interview and/or survey is a graduation requirement; students apply for graduation in the final spring. (5) DISCREPANCY DISCLOSED: the Plan of Study PDF hosted on catalog.usf.edu itself (mime/media/23/6733, same program/catalog) sums to 122 credits (its Semester 5 has two 3-cr unrestricted electives where the College plan places EGN 2440 plus a 4-cr 6AC general elective, and its final semester lists 15 credits vs the College plan's 12), contradicting the catalog's own 120-credit degree total. This JSON follows the College of Engineering's plan, which sums exactly to 120 as printed. (6) Major elective example courses are real entries from the catalog's approved elective lists; theory options are COT 4210, COT 4521, COT 4601 per the catalog. (7) Prereq arrays left empty; consult the catalog course inventory for per-course prerequisites.",
